---
import Sub from '../layouts/Sub.astro';
import { cityPageSchema, SERVICE_PAGES } from '../data/site.js';

const description =
  'Concrete sealing in Hurricane, Utah — driveways, patios, pool decks, garage floors and asphalt out to Sand Hollow. Based in St. George, free on-site assessment.';

const schema = cityPageSchema({
  path: '/concrete-sealing-hurricane-ut',
  city: 'Hurricane',
  description,
});
---

<Sub
  title="Concrete Sealing in Hurricane, UT | Armour Crete"
  description={description}
  crumb="Hurricane, UT"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Fragment slot="h1">Concrete sealing<br />in Hurricane.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Hurricane concrete lives a hard life — full desert exposure on the way out to
    Sand Hollow, salt pools in the backyards, and garage floors that work for a
    living. We seal all of it with named Deco products, and the assessment is
    free anywhere in town.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>24h</dt><dd>Cure before the surface is back in use</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Deco</dt><dd>The only products we put down</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Free</dt><dd>On-site assessment, anywhere in Hurricane</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Services in Hurricane, UT</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Everything we do,<br />done here.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="chips rv">
        {SERVICE_PAGES.map((s) => <li><a href={s.href}>{s.label}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
      <div class="prose rv" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <p>
          Driveways and patios get the penetrating-sealer treatment;
          <a class="tlink" href="/pool-deck-sealing">pool decks</a> get the
          salt-specific product; garage floors that hold vehicles, tools and toys
          get sealed so they wipe down instead of staining. Hurricane also has
          more <a class="tlink" href="/asphalt-sealing">asphalt drives and
          lanes</a> than most of the county, and ours is the no-tar way to bring
          those back.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="rv">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-lt">The local physics</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Full exposure,<br />no shade to hide in.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose rv">
        <p>
          Out here the sun does most of the damage and the winter nights finish
          it. An exposed slab swings through more than a hundred degrees across
          the year; the movement opens hairline cracks, water and salt follow
          them in, and freeze–thaw plus salt crystallisation break the surface
          from the inside. Unsealed concrete in full exposure simply runs that
          cycle faster than concrete that gets any shade at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          A penetrating sealer keeps the pore network from staying saturated —
          which is the whole game. Prep first where the surface needs it,
          <a class="tlink" href="/expansion-joint-replacement">joints re-filled</a>
          where they have failed, and the right product for the exposure rather
          than one product for everything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hurricane questions</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Asked in<br />Hurricane.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq rv">
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Do you really come out to Hurricane for a free assessment?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Yes. We are based in St. George and Hurricane is squarely inside our
            home patch — the visit is free and carries no obligation.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Can you do the pool deck and the driveway in one job?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            That is the usual arrangement. They take different products — the
            deck gets the salt-specific sealer, the driveway the clear
            penetrating one — but one visit, one scope, one cure day.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>How long is the surface out of action?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Twenty-four hours for concrete. Asphalt dries faster, and we give you
            the exact window when we see the surface.
          </p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Sub>
